<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ismail Omar Guelleh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ismail Omar Guelleh is a Djiboutian politician who has been president of Djibouti since 1999, succeeding his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hassan-gouled-aptidon">Hassan Gouled Aptidon</a>. A former head of the security services, he has won repeated elections dominated by his ruling coalition. His government has developed the port and the railway to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a> and leased bases to foreign powers, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ismail-omar-guelleh.jpg" alt="Ismail Omar Guelleh" width="330" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Secretary of Defense · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Djiboutian_President_Ismail_Omar_Guelleh_at_the_presidential_palace_in_Djibouti,_Republic_of_Djibouti,_September_24,_2023_-_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Ismail Omar Guelleh</b> succeeded Gouled in 1999 and has held office since.</blockquote><a href="/state/djibouti">Djibouti</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Dire Dawa, in what is now <a href="/countries/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=9.58,41.87&amp;year=1982" aria-label="Dire Dawa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5705 1806 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ismail Omar Guelleh"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6155 2076h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6155 2076h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=9.58,41.87&amp;year=1982">What was here in 1982? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
